  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions",
    "Past participle: *chutado* (regular)",
    "Informal sports term borrowed from English \"to shoot,\" most common in football/soccer contexts — *chutó el balón a la portería* (he shot the ball at the goal)",
    "Common colloquial expression: *¡y chuta!* = \"and that's that!\" / \"and there you go!\" (used dismissively, like throwing something and being done with it)",
